From 1a70bb840e6cfaf1395eb0844caf26fe56314719 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 08:14:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 085/145] media: meson: vdec: hevc: never program an
 out-of-range FBC chunk

codec_hevc_fill_mmu_map() indexes comm->fbc_chunks[vb->index][] with
i / FBC_CHUNK_PAGES for i over nb_pages, and dereferences the result to
build the page map the decoder then DMAs through.

nb_pages and fbc_nr_chunks are both derived from the session geometry, but
at different times - the chunk array is allocated in
codec_hevc_setup_buffers() and reused whenever it is already present,
while nb_pages is recomputed on every frame. Nothing checks that the two
still agree, and nothing checks the entry is non-NULL.

The failure mode if they ever disagree is unusually nasty: the loop reads
past the array, treats whatever it finds as a struct fbc_chunk, and writes
that object's "paddr >> PAGE_SHIFT" into the map as a page frame number.
The hardware then DMAs frame data to that physical address. The corruption
lands in whoever owns that memory, arbitrarily far from this driver and
long after the fact - a crash in USB interrupt completion, say - and no CPU
memory checker can attribute it, because the write is done by the decoder.

Bound the index and reject a NULL chunk, failing the frame rather than
mapping something we do not own. Both branches are ratelimited dev_err, so
if this ever fires it names itself instead of corrupting silently.

Signed-off-by: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
---
 .../media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc_common.c      | 30 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc_common.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc_common.c
index 31947f0171ec..606e7112f603 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc_common.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc_common.c
@@ -607,8 +607,34 @@ void codec_hevc_fill_mmu_map(struct amvdec_session *sess,
 
 	if (comm->fbc_chunks[vb->index]) {
 		for (i = 0; i < nb_pages; ++i) {
-			struct fbc_chunk *c =
-				comm->fbc_chunks[vb->index][i / FBC_CHUNK_PAGES];
+			u32 ci = i / FBC_CHUNK_PAGES;
+			struct fbc_chunk *c;
+
+			/*
+			 * nb_pages and fbc_nr_chunks are derived from the
+			 * session geometry at two different times.  If they
+			 * ever disagree, this walks off the chunk array and
+			 * programs whatever it finds as a page frame number -
+			 * and the decoder then DMAs into that physical
+			 * address.  The damage lands in whatever owns that
+			 * memory, arbitrarily far from this driver, so fail
+			 * the frame instead.
+			 */
+			if (ci >= comm->fbc_nr_chunks) {
+				dev_err_ratelimited(sess->core->dev,
+					"FBC chunk %u >= %u (nb_pages %u, buf %u) - refusing to map\n",
+					ci, comm->fbc_nr_chunks, nb_pages,
+					vb->index);
+				break;
+			}
+
+			c = comm->fbc_chunks[vb->index][ci];
+			if (!c) {
+				dev_err_ratelimited(sess->core->dev,
+					"FBC chunk %u of buffer %u is NULL - refusing to map\n",
+					ci, vb->index);
+				break;
+			}
 
 			mmu_map[i] = (c->paddr >> PAGE_SHIFT) +
 				     (i % FBC_CHUNK_PAGES);
-- 
